/K [11]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 676 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the LED pin as an OUTPUT using pinMode\(\).)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 677 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It uses digitalWrite\(\) to keep the LED pin HIGH, which keeps the LED turned ON.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 678 0 R
/E (When the rocker switch is connected in series with the LED's power supply, turning the switch ON allows current to flow and the LED glows continuously. Turning the switch OFF cuts the power, and the LED turns OFF.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (So overall, the rocker switch acts as a manual ON/OFF control for the LED.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
